---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ScreenshotSlot from '../../components/ScreenshotSlot.astro';
import GamingModes from '../../components/GamingModes.astro';
import WorkshopLinks from '../../components/WorkshopLinks.astro';
import art from '../../assets/projects/ai-gaming.png';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<SiteLayout title="AI Gaming" description="AI Gaming 0.4.0 is a Development preview of player-confirmed Ollama Local advice. Companion packaging and in-game behavior are not verified." path="ai-gaming/" active="mods">
	<section class="hero page-wrap">
		<div class="hero-copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">Mod 03 · Development preview 0.4.0</p>
			<h1>AI Gaming</h1>
			<p class="hero-lead">The 0.4.0 Development source adds an optional Windows companion for Ollama Local advice. Choose which aggregate city details to share, write a question, review the complete request and confirm it each time. Replies are advice only; this preview does not control the simulation.</p>
			<div class="status-strip"><span class="tag">Ollama Local</span><span class="tag">Confirm every request</span><span class="tag">Package and runtime pending</span><span class="tag">English · 繁體中文</span></div>
			<WorkshopLinks mod="ai-gaming" />
		</div>
		<figure class="hero-art"><Image src={art} alt="AI Gaming artwork" widths={[560, 720]} sizes="(max-width: 640px) 100vw, 45vw" format="webp" quality={78} loading="eager" /><figcaption class="art-note">Project artwork · not a gameplay screenshot</figcaption></figure>
	</section>

	<nav class="subnav page-wrap" aria-label="AI Gaming guide"><a href={base + 'wiki/ai-gaming/overview/'}>Guide</a><a href={base + 'wiki/project/roadmap/'}>Roadmap</a></nav>

	<section class="section soft">
		<div class="page-wrap columns">
			<div class="text-stack">
				<p class="eyebrow">Current Development source</p>
				<h2>Review every request before confirming it.</h2>
				<p>The settings page lets you choose which aggregate city fields to include: game date, population, funds, residential demand, commercial demand and workplace demand. All six start selected, so remove any fields you do not want to share. Add a model name and your question, then review the complete preview before sending.</p>
				<p>The separate city-summary command remains available; it writes the game date, population and funds to the local game log when you request it.</p>
				<p>Each request needs a separate confirmation. The response is displayed as advice only; it is not interpreted as a game action. The source has no cloud-provider adapter or API-key entry.</p>
				<p>AI Gaming sends the selected information to Ollama on this PC. Ollama may route inference to a cloud service depending on its own configuration, which the mod cannot inspect. Do not include city names, account information, secrets or personal data in the free-text question.</p>
				<p class="section-intro"><strong>Package and runtime status:</strong> The Development upload job completed, but final Steam processing has not been verified. A self-contained Windows x64 companion package, the Cities: Skylines runtime and actual Ollama requests also remain unverified. The source defaults to <code>CompanionSha256=UNCONFIGURED</code> and refuses to launch an unverified companion, so this feature should not yet be treated as ready for use.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="screenshot-stack">
				<ScreenshotSlot title="Ollama request preview" description="The selected city fields, model name, question and separate confirmation control." />
				<ScreenshotSlot title="Advice response" description="The model response displayed as advice, without changing the simulation." />
				<ScreenshotSlot title="City summary in the log" description="The separate manual summary with the game date, population and funds." />
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="interactive-section"><div class="page-wrap"><p class="section-label">The idea · three ways to play</p><h2>How you and the AI could share a city.</h2><GamingModes locale="en" /></div></section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="page-wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">Roadmap and safeguards</p>
			<h2>You stay in control.</h2>
			<div class="roadmap"><article><strong>1 · Observe</strong><p>Selected aggregate city data is available in the Development source.</p></article><article><strong>2 · Suggest</strong><p>0.4.0 source adds player-confirmed Ollama Local advice; package and runtime checks are pending.</p></article><article><strong>3 · Act, with permission</strong><p>Game actions are not implemented and remain planned.</p></article></div>
			<p class="section-intro">The long-term design is to use capabilities from other Modpack mods instead of duplicating them. Version 0.4.0 contains no interop calls, cloud-provider adapters or gameplay actions.</p>
			<a class="text-link" href={base + 'wiki/project/roadmap/'}>Full roadmap →</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</SiteLayout>
<!-- Updated by OpenAI-Codex on 2026-10-26. -->
